  "term": "Calvinism",
  "definition": "Calvinism is the theological system associated with John Calvin. In this historical account, it presents human life within a divine plan in which God’s will, predestination, sin, grace, and salvation are central, including the idea that humanity shares in Adam’s fall and that salvation comes through union with Christ by faith.",
